Missing/empty sections: Elevate these to the Checks & Warnings.

<50-word sections: Produce minimal summaries that acknowledge insufficiency.

Hallucination mitigation: Disallow speculative claims; use “the text states…” style when needed.

Long-paper chunking (PS2):

Chunk criteria: If a section exceeds context capacity, split by natural boundaries (subheadings, paragraphs).

Local summaries: Summarize chunks in order.

Constrained merge: Combine chunk summaries without adding new claims.
